//! Physical-write golden (appender_write_path_PLAN.md D11, narrowed by
//! critique C12): a fixed, deterministic operation script is driven through
//! `history::write_value` / `delete_value` (inside `with_write_txn`) and
//! through `api::commit_changes`, then every row of every value, `_hist` and
//! axis table, the `commit` log (without its wall-clock `timestamp`) and the
//! sequences' counters are rendered **in Rust** and compared with
//! `tests/fixtures/write_path_golden.txt`.
//!
//! The fixture was generated by the multi-placeholder `VALUES` write path
//! (before the columnar-bind switch) and must match unchanged after it: the
//! golden pins the physical bytes the writer produces, so any change to how a
//! row reaches DuckDB that alters a stored value fails here.
//!
//! Rendering never goes through DuckDB's `::VARCHAR` (its float formatting is
//! engine-version dependent): floats render as `f64::to_bits` hex, timestamps
//! as epoch µs, strings Rust-escaped, lists element-wise (a list longer than
//! 64 elements renders as its length plus an FNV-1a hash of its rendered
//! elements, to keep the fixture small). Values stay small (≤ ~1 100 cells,
//! still crossing the old 512-row chunk); large shapes are structural tests
//! elsewhere, not golden rows. Physical rows only, no read-macro outputs:
//! physical identity implies read identity, and the read suites cover reads.
//!
//! Regenerate ONLY with `NODAL_REGEN_GOLDEN=1 cargo test -p nodal-db-core
//! --test write_path_golden`, and give the reason in the commit message. A
//! schema change is expected to show up here (review-visible by design).

